# SealedSecret TEMPLATE — selection-list-secrets (S14 / FFRNT-200)
#
# ============================================================================
# THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE. IT CONTAINS NO SECRET AND IS NOT APPLIED.
# ============================================================================
#
# selection-list-service has its OWN Postgres database (fuzefront_selection_list)
# and its OWN login role (selection_list_svc). This Secret holds that role's
# password and NOTHING ELSE. Full pattern + rotation + threat model:
#   docs/runbooks/per-service-database-and-role.md
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT HAND-MINT OR HAND-SEAL THE PASSWORD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The value must never be seen by a human or an agent. Mint + seal it with the
# dispatchable workflow, which generates it in-run from `openssl rand`, seals it
# OFFLINE against the committed public cert and opens a PR containing only
# ciphertext:
#
#   gh workflow run rotate-sealed-secret.yml \
#     -f scope=fuzefront/selection-list-secrets \
#     -f key=DB_PASSWORD \
#     -f manifest=deploy/contabo/sealed/selection-list-secrets.yaml
#
# (The workflow creates the manifest when it does not exist yet. Review + merge
# the resulting PR in a deploy window; Argo's `fuzefront-sealed` app applies it.)
#
# The result is the file below with real ciphertext in place of the placeholder.
# Commit ONLY that output - NEVER plaintext.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secret keys consumed by templates/selection-list-service-deployment.yaml and
# templates/service-db-bootstrap-job.yaml (DB password only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   DB_PASSWORD   — password of the selection_list_svc role. Read by the
#                   pre-sync bootstrap Job (creates/reconciles the role with this
#                   password) AND by the Deployment (DB_PASSWORD env). The
#                   service connects with DB_HOST/DB_PORT/DB_NAME/DB_USER/DB_PASSWORD
#                   (DATABASE_URL is deliberately not used).
#
#   JWT_SECRET is NOT in this Secret: the Deployment reads the shared platform
#   JWT secret from fuzefront-secrets, like chat-service and devportal-service.
#
#   SERVICE_CLIENT_ID / SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET are NOT in this Secret any more.
#                   The service's OWN OAuth client_credentials identity (scope
#                   `authz:admin`, used for Security API grant/revoke) is minted
#                   IN-CLUSTER by the selection-list-s2s-register PreSync Job
#                   (templates/selection-list-s2s-register-job.yaml, gated by
#                   selectionListService.s2s.register.enabled, on in
#                   values-prod.yaml) and published as a SEPARATE Secret,
#                   Secret/selection-list-s2s (keys AUTHENTIK_CLIENT_ID /
#                   AUTHENTIK_CLIENT_SECRET). Nothing to seal, no credential-handoff,
#                   no human ever sees the value. It must be separate: this Secret
#                   is owned by the sealed-secrets controller, which replaces it on
#                   reconcile, so a key a Job wrote here would silently vanish.
#                   See docs/runbooks/s2s-client-credentials.md. (If you must
#                   provide the identity out of band instead, publish a Secret named
#                   selectionListService.s2s.secretName with those two keys and
#                   leave s2s.register.enabled=false.)
#
# NOTE: selection-list-service's authorization is routed through FuzeFront's
# own Security API (SECURITY_SERVICE_URL, a plain in-cluster Service DNS value)
# - there is no PERMIT_API_KEY here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GO-LIVE sequence (two separate merges - ORDER MATTERS)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   1. Dispatch the workflow above; merge its PR. Argo applies the SealedSecret
#      and the controller decrypts it into Secret/selection-list-secrets.
#   2. ONLY THEN flip `selectionListService.enabled: true` in values-prod.yaml.
#      The bootstrap Job is a pre-upgrade hook that runs BEFORE the sealed-secret
#      sync, so enabling both in one change fails the Job on a missing Secret
#      (which fails the whole sync).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rotation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Re-dispatch the same workflow. The next Argo sync of the chart re-runs the
#   bootstrap Job, which ALTERs the role to the new password; then restart the
#   service pods so they pick it up (see the runbook).
#
---
# Replace the entire block below with the sealing workflow's output.
apiVersion: bitnami.com/v1alpha1
kind: SealedSecret
metadata:
  name: selection-list-secrets
  namespace: fuzefront
spec:
  encryptedData:
    # Replace with sealed ciphertext. Do NOT commit plaintext.
    DB_PASSWORD: <REPLACE_WITH_KUBESEAL_OUTPUT>
  template:
    metadata:
      name: selection-list-secrets
      namespace: fuzefront
    type: Opaque
